# Attribute-style possessive relations - rendered "X's gender is ...".
# Kind-valued targets, rendered by KIND in :NP. nationality is NOT here -
# it is rendered by the dedicated bare-is template ("X is english") in
# Statements.mgr; keeping it in :REL too would let the longer possessive
# phrase outsort the bare-is form (see the greedy lexicon sort).
"gender"                gender                  .
"social class"          class-situation         .
